WEBVTT

00:05.800 --> 00:08.360
Why does an organization do a project.

00:08.590 --> 00:12.790
Well that question is called the project initiation context.

00:12.820 --> 00:15.040
We'll see it again coming up.

00:15.040 --> 00:19.860
The reason why projects are generally selected why an organization does a project.

00:19.900 --> 00:27.640
Is there some business value for initiating a project for investing the time and the money and the resources

00:28.060 --> 00:32.640
into the effort to create that unique product service condition or result.

00:33.030 --> 00:37.200
Well that value is called business value a business.

00:37.200 --> 00:45.280
Now you describe the benefits for the organization or the stakeholders or the customers of the project.

00:45.340 --> 00:51.640
So organizations do projects because projects enable business value.

00:51.640 --> 00:55.460
There are two types of business now you have tangible business value.

00:55.540 --> 01:01.990
And of course intangible tangibles easy to see we're talking about things you get new fixtures or equipment

01:01.990 --> 01:10.990
or hardware software money you get you get a profit from the project you get a market share your stakeholders

01:11.020 --> 01:12.220
get some equity.

01:12.220 --> 01:17.440
So it's all those those good things you can touch and feel and there's utility to that money or to that

01:17.440 --> 01:18.950
equity or what have you.

01:19.390 --> 01:25.720
So those are tangible now in tangible business now you are things like Goodwill and reputation in the

01:25.720 --> 01:27.790
community or in the marketplace.

01:28.000 --> 01:34.630
Brand recognition is there's a public benefit so it's like a not for profit or a project that was done

01:34.630 --> 01:35.830
for the community.

01:35.860 --> 01:41.230
So there's a public benefit could be trademarks or strategic alignment.

01:41.440 --> 01:46.700
So those are intangible hard to quantify the value of brand recognition.

01:46.870 --> 01:50.860
So but you could do a project to increase your brand recognition.

01:51.100 --> 01:56.510
But that's business now you will see business value a couple times throughout the course.

01:56.620 --> 02:01.810
Generally business value is described in a document called the business case.

02:01.810 --> 02:05.220
The business case of course describes why do we want to do this project.

02:05.230 --> 02:07.050
Why do we want to invest in it.

02:07.090 --> 02:09.880
So what is the return on investment.

02:09.940 --> 02:16.020
And that's where we described business now the work that your project creates for the organization.

02:16.480 --> 02:17.470
All right great job.

02:17.470 --> 02:18.820
Keep moving forward.
